B.ctO=new A.d1("splitpane","A LIVE, table-backed dashboard splitter: one resizable pane per row of `table`. Panes are DATA \u2014 add a row to add a pane, hide a row (visibleColumn=false) to break one down, drag a divider to re-weight (persisted to weightColumn). Each pane content comes from its kindColumn value via `paneKinds` (kind -> child node). Desktop = a resizable Row/Column; phone = swipeable tabs. A `map`/`glmap` paneKind is offered in the view switcher and per-panel editor only when its geo config actually resolves (inline geojson/geojsonAsset, or a table whose schema has both lat/lon columns, or a bare-tiles glmap); an unsatisfiable one is hidden from both pickers and a row already on one falls back to a plain label instead of erroring. Use as a split/fill-rooted screen body (needs bounded height).",B.beC,!1)
