B.ctM=new A.d1("noms","Opens on a TITLE MENU (New game/Custom/Single player/Multiplayer/Settings/Info) over the gameplay dimmed. A controllable real-time RTS: pan/zoom a world, TAP-select or BOX-select noms and command them (move/attack). DESIGN THE FLOW by painting ZONES (Gather/Grow/Guard/Home) with a per-zone flow target \u2014 noms self-organise to fill them and ferry food into a shared GRANARY. MOVE the tribe with \ud83d\udccd Rally flags (one tap each, no selecting; drop several and each nom heads to the nearest). GAME MODES: open-ended Sandbox (harmony/domination are celebrations, not game-enders) or a timed Speed Run. BUILD A CITY: place blueprints of fictional-tech buildings (burrow/glow-post/larder/moot-hall) and the noms construct them from granary food \u2014 finished buildings cheer + speed the town. Set POLICIES (share food, cooperate, build tunnels, self-control, or delegate to the noms) \u2014 and balance the society: both scarcity AND abundance breed greed, violence and DEVOLUTION, so aim for the middle. A coach hint, pause/speed and a balance meter keep it legible. Dig water to grow trees; miracles noms LEARN; two tribes fight. A CULTURE SIM: each nom carries a cultural identity + values that spread to neighbours, inherit across generations and DIVERGE into distinct cultures (toggle the culture view to see them). Cultures CLASH or BLEND at their borders and grow traits \u2014 a Rite of Sharing or a Taboo of Hoarding \u2014 that shape how they share and cooperate (the culture view shows the seams). AUTOPLAY: an auto-keeper (\ud83e\udd16) grows a thriving, balanced colony itself \u2014 digs water, populates, lays zones, tunes policies and builds. A \ud83d\udcac LIVE NARRATION feed explains what is happening and WHY (every autoplay decision states its reason), an adjustable SPEED control fast-forwards 1\xd7\u21928\xd7 (sub-stepped so it stays stable), and a one-tap FULL AUTO-RUN starts a self-running, narrated, fast-forwarded society to just sit back and watch. Seed-based reproducible worlds. Touch + mouse + web.",B.bBl,!1)
B.cS1=new A.p("seed",B.af,"World seed - same seed reproduces the same resource field.",B.f,null)
B.cQN=new A.p("saveTable",B.at,'Table holding campaign save rows (default "campaign").',B.f,null)
B.bix=s([B.cS1,B.cQN],t.G)
B.cuj=new A.d1("spacegame","TETHERFIELD - a real-time build-a-power-grid, mine, and defend game (an original homage to the classic The Space Game). Drop MODULES into a resource field; they AUTO-LINK to neighbours within range to form a power web. GENERATORS make energy, RELAYS carry power + minerals across the web, CELLS bank it, EXTRACTORS on deposits turn power into minerals, and TURRETS (Laser / Pulser / Beam / Lance - each with its own range, the Lance with a MIN range so it cannot hit point-blank) auto-target and defend the CORE against escalating waves of enemies (Darts, Breakers, beam-resistant Toruses, and a Colossus boss). Links GLOW when power flows. Modes: Campaign (a mission chain with objective panel + progress bar, Next-level / Replay / Retry flow, and in-session completion ticks on the mission list), Survival (endless), and Sandbox (free build). Tap to place, Sell to remove for a partial refund. In-memory sandbox.",B.bix,!1)
B.cUr=new A.p("seed",B.af,"Simulation seed - same seed reproduces the same wave pattern.",B.f,null)
B.bg7=s([B.cUr],t.G)
B.cuJ=new A.d1("hesset","HESSET - a GEOMETRY strategy/defense game where the player DRAWS the geometry (deliberately unlike spacegame: no auto-linking). Place shape-NODES - triangle Spikes (shoot at foes), square Anchors (cheap, tough, structural), pentagon Wells (generate FLUX, the single resource), hexagon Prisms (amplifiers) - and DRAG an edge from one shape to another (cost grows with length, capped). CLOSING a loop of edges claims the enclosed polygon as a live FIELD whose role comes from the majority shape in its ring: Spike loops KILL foes inside, Well loops earn flux by AREA, Anchor loops are BASTIONS (the ring resists damage), Prism loops are RESONANT (boost adjacent fields). Hostile shapes attack from the rim - Shards saw through edges, Orbs ram nodes, the slow Mass grinds toward the CORE you must protect. Objectives include the signature CLAIM goal (total enclosed area) and survive-N-waves. Modes: Campaign (teaches one shape at a time), Endless, and Sandbox. Tap to place, drag to draw, Sell to remove for a partial refund. Minimal luminous look. In-memory sandbox.",B.bg7,!1)
B.cId=new A.p("cols",B.af,"Hex columns (default 22).",B.f,null)
