B.cY1=new A.p("action",B.X,'Action spec { fn, args } fired on debounced change and on submit; any literal "$value" in args (nested lists/maps included) is substituted with the field\'s current text first.',B.f,null)
B.bqM=s([B.cPM,B.cIh,B.cY1],t.G)
B.cui=new A.d1("textinput",'A single-line free-text field \u2014 the `slider` $value-substitution pattern generalized from numeric to text. On every change (debounced) AND on submit (immediate) it can fire an `action` (any literal "$value" in args, however deeply nested, is substituted with the field\'s current text first \u2014 an empty field still fires, so a "clear" is expressible). No table binding of its own; drives whatever action the applet author wires (e.g. a debounced search-as-you-type `http` fetch).',B.bqM,!1)
