B.cGs=new A.p("linksTable",B.at,"Enables Obsidian-style `[[Title]]` wiki-links: an auto-maintained link-row index in this table (add/remove/update on every save), tappable resolved-link spans in Preview (writes `sel:<table>` \u2014 pair with an explorer's `followSelection` to jump there), and a `[[` title autocomplete while typing. Unset (default) \u2192 zero behavior change. If a merge (or any external write) ever leaves two linksTable rows with the same resolved title for the same FROM note, the sync keeps the FIRST row in table order and reaps the rest \u2014 deterministic, not arbitrary.",B.f,null)
B.cXA=new A.p("linkFromColumn",B.t,'linksTable column holding the FROM note\'s id (default "fromId").',B.f,null)
B.cVo=new A.p("linkToColumn",B.t,'linksTable column holding the resolved TO note\'s id, empty when unresolved (default "toId").',B.f,null)
B.cGQ=new A.p("linkTitleColumn",B.t,'linksTable column holding the link\'s literal target title text, kept even when unresolved (default "toTitle").',B.f,null)
B.cRb=new A.p("linkFromTitleColumn",B.t,'linksTable column that also receives the FROM note\'s own title (default "fromTitle") \u2014 kept in sync on every wiki-link sync pass and on rename of the source note. Lets a backlinks view label each row with the source without a join.',B.f,null)
B.cVy=new A.p("onLinkTap",B.X,"Opt-in action spec { fn, args } fired when a plain Markdown `[label](target)` link (NOT a `[[Title]]` wiki-link, which uses linksTable instead) is tapped in Preview. `target` (the link's raw url/title text) substitutes any literal \"$value\" in args, same as textinput's action. Unset (default) \u2192 the link renders styled but inert, unchanged from before this prop existed.",B.f,null)
B.cLw=new A.p("lazyBlocks",B.U,"Opt-in LAZY read view: builds only on-screen Markdown blocks (ListView.builder) instead of the default eager build-everything-up-front view. For a genuinely long document (e.g. a full encyclopedia article) this is the fix for visible scroll lag. No effect when `readOnly`'s shrinkWrap (inline preview) applies. Off by default \u2014 zero behavior change for existing callers.",B.f,null)
B.cKq=new A.p("jumpToSectionSetting",B.D,'Opt-in "jump to section" (only acts when lazyBlocks is also true): names a board-settings key. When that setting\'s value changes to "<anything>::<heading text>" (the leading part just needs to change to force a re-jump on a repeated tap of the same section \u2014 e.g. a timestamp), the read view animate-scrolls to the first #/##/### heading block matching the text (trimmed, case-insensitive) at an ESTIMATED position \u2014 not pixel-exact.',B.f,null)
B.cGO=new A.p("findEnabledSetting",B.D,'Opt-in "Find in article" (only acts when lazyBlocks is also true): names a board-settings key an external affordance (e.g. a \u22ee "Find in article" action) toggles true/false to open/close an inline search bar rendered above the article. The typed query, per-occurrence match highlighting, match-count feedback ("N of M"), next/prev stepping and scroll-to-match are all self-contained in this widget \u2014 no other prop or host wiring is needed. Plain case-insensitive substring matching only, no regex, no cross-block spans. Unset (default) \u2192 zero behavior change.',B.f,null)
B.cGi=new A.p("serifH1",B.U,"Opt-in encyclopedia-style DISPLAY TITLE: renders a top-level `# ` Markdown heading in a serif font stack (Georgia / Times New Roman / Noto Serif / generic serif fallback \u2014 no new font asset bundled, so this always renders with whatever serif face the platform already has) instead of the body sans-serif, at a larger display size. Applies to every `# ` heading in the document (in practice just the one at the very top \u2014 see `document`) in BOTH the eager and `lazyBlocks` read-view paths. Off by default: zero behavior change for every existing caller.",B.f,null)
B.cG1=new A.p("imagesTable",B.at,"Enables `local:<id>` resolution for a standalone `![alt](src)` image block (and gives inline `![alt](src)` mid-paragraph a real target to resolve, though inline never promotes to a block): the id looks up a row in this table, whose imageSrcColumn holds a base64 payload rendered via the engine's existing local-bytes image path (same as `record`'s image preview) \u2014 never fetched. An http(s) src, or a `local:<id>` that doesn't resolve, always renders as alt text; this node has no image-fetch code at all. Unset (default) \u2192 zero behavior change.",B.f,null)
B.cHv=new A.p("imageSrcColumn",B.t,'Column on imagesTable holding the base64 image payload (default "b64").',B.f,null)
