B.cPF=new A.p("bare",B.U,"Render the child WITHOUT its own top-level chrome (a `header` or `backbutton` at the top of the embedded body) \u2014 for a host surface that already draws a header and would otherwise stack two. The resolver can ask for the same thing by returning an EmbeddedApplet with `chrome: false`; either side asking is enough. Default false = today's behavior, byte-identical.",B.f,null)
B.cIf=new A.p("scope",B.X,'Optional `{table, rowId}` to open the embedded applet ALREADY SCOPED to one row (e.g. `{"table":"boards","rowId":"..."}`) \u2014 reuses the child applet\'s OWN `scopeTargets` (the same explorer-driven scoping a user gets by picking that row), so the embed opens with no unscoped list flash. Absent = unscoped default screen (unchanged behavior).',B.f,null)
B.cXS=new A.p("height",B.af,"Slot height in px (default 520); set for taller/shorter embeds.",B.f,null)
B.cUx=new A.p("width",B.af,"Optional fixed width; omit to fill the available width.",B.f,null)
B.cTp=new A.p("presetScope",B.X,"priorun-0802 unit2: `{table, column, value}` \u2014 directly calls BoardState.setScope(table, column, value) on the CHILD board so any scopeColumn-aware node inside it (e.g. bubl's `scopeColumn`) filters by that column, with no scopeTargets declaration needed. Distinct from `scope` above (opens on one specific row via the child's OWN declared scopeTargets). `value` supports the same live-token convention every filter-shaped prop uses ($rowId = this embed own injected row, $selected:<table> = the host board live selection, $playerId, or a literal). FAIL-CLOSED: a configured-but-unresolved token (nothing selected yet) sets the scope to a sentinel matching no real row \u2014 never falls back to unscoped \u2014 unless `scopeOptional: true` is also set. Absent = no setScope call at all (unchanged default).",B.f,null)
B.cKS=new A.p("scopeOptional",B.U,'Pairs with `presetScope` only. Default false keeps presetScope fail-closed (unresolved token -> sentinel, empty scoped set). Set true to instead CLEAR the scope on an unresolved token (full unscoped child) \u2014 for a user-driven selection-chip use where "nothing selected yet" should show everything, not nothing. Mirrors priolanes\' `scopeOptional`.',B.f,null)
